C03: a proper title after «poné» plays on YouTube in the local player (VIDEO1715)

«poné Tom and Jerry» (H0486) reached no operation: the music readers required a music noun or an «X de Y» shape. A title written with the person's own capitals — at least two capitalised words joined only by connectors, no digits, not a known application name — after poné/pon/play is now what to play; with no provider named it goes to media.play.youtube in the local player, as provider-less music has since MUSIC1559. The resolver hands the raw text to the music readers so the capitals survive folding, and a title «en Disney+/Netflix/Prime/HBO/Max/Crunchyroll/Star/Paramount/Twitch/Hulu/Peacock» stays that service's session, never YouTube (the registry rows «pon Daredevil en Disney+» and «pon The Mandalorian en Disney Plus» are unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


